# TypeScript Strict Enforcement — AEC-V-2026-03

## 1. COMPILER REQUIREMENTS

tsconfig.json must include:

- "strict": true
- "noImplicitAny": true
- "strictNullChecks": true

Zero errors tolerated.

---

## 2. PROHIBITIONS

- any (explicit or implicit)
- untyped props
- mutable physics constants

---

## 3. BRANDED PHYSICS TYPES (MANDATORY)

```ts
declare const BRAND_WAVELENGTH: unique symbol;
declare const BRAND_LUMINANCE: unique symbol;

export type Wavelength = number & { [BRAND_WAVELENGTH]: true };
export type Luminance = number & { [BRAND_LUMINANCE]: true };
4. CONSTANT ENFORCEMENT
export const LUMA_CONSTANTS = {
  wavelength: 520 as Wavelength,
  luminance: 300 as Luminance,
  albedo: 0.05,
  acquisitionLatency: 0.8
} as const;
readonly required
no runtime mutation
5. COMPONENT RULES

All components must:

use typed props via interface
avoid default any inference
avoid unnecessary state
6. DATA FLOW
physics constants imported only from:
→ /types/physics.d.ts
no duplication allowed
7. FORBIDDEN PATTERNS
magic numbers (except branded constants)
inline physics values
unit ambiguity (nm vs px etc.)
8. RENDER DISCIPLINE

React is used for:

structure
composition

NOT for:

physics simulation
lighting logic